# A CRLF `sh` script breaks under CI/WSL and in heredocs — the shell is the one tool whose
# line endings are not cosmetic. PowerShell's parser accepts both, but CRLF is its native form
# and what `Set-Content`/`Out-File` write, so a normalization pass never fights the OS.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
